 # #614 十四张无佐证 reviewed 卡批量补审（欧阳锋）
Root cause found. The original frontmatter value: `decision_source: #613 上报王语嫣的...` — starts with `#` which in YAML is a comment! So `yaml.safe_load` parses `decision_source:` with value None (the `#613 ...` is a comment). So the round-trip via safe_load + safe_dump wipes it. It's not really the script "erasing" — it's that the original YAML was malformed (unquoted value starting with #), and claim's parse→dump normalizes it to null.

  But from the factory's perspective, the fix per the task: "修法：claim/complete 回写只动状态字段，保留其余非空字段。" — i.e., write-side should preserve the original raw lines for fields not being updated, rather than parse→dump round-trip. That handles any YAML quirks (unquoted #, anchors, weird formatting).

  Minimal fix approach for `update_task_frontmatter`: instead of yaml round-trip, do line-level editing — parse the frontmatter text lines, update only the keys in updates (plus updated_at), preserve all other lines verbatim. If a key in updates doesn't exist, append it. That keeps everything else byte-identical.

  Also #613 title wiped — same mechanism presumably (`title: ...` starting with #? Actually #613's title might start with "排查..." hmm. Whatever — line-preserving write fixes the class).

  Edge cases for line-based edit:
  - Multi-line YAML values (e.g., list or folded scalar) — must preserve the whole block of non-updated keys, and when updating an existing key, replace only its line if single-line; if existing value spans multiple lines, we need to replace the block. Keep it simple: when updating an existing key, if the next lines are continuation lines (indented), remove them and write the new value inline (safe_dump scalar).
  - Keys to add: insert before closing `---`.

  Also must handle the case where frontmatter missing/malformed — fall back to old behavior? Current code returns {} when no match. Keep a fallback: if regex doesn't match, use old path.

  Actually let me write a surgical `update_task_frontmatter` that:

  ```python
